id: quiz.k8s.zero-downtime
kind: quiz
track: kubernetes
title: Deploying without downtime
question: How would you deploy a new version of a service without dropping requests?
expects:
  - rolling update
  - readiness probe
  - maxsurge
  - graceful shutdown
  - migration
misuse:
  - readiness equals liveness => readiness that restarts pods instead of gating traffic
  - no drain => in-flight requests fail on every deploy
related:
  - k8s.deployment.rolling-update
  - k8s.probe.readiness
  - design.graceful-shutdown
  - design.schema-migration
follow_ups:
  - the new version fails after 30% of traffic moved -- what now?
  - how does the database schema fit into this?
answer: |
  Rolling update with maxSurge/maxUnavailable; new pods must become Ready before
  old ones are removed; graceful shutdown with preStop/terminationGracePeriod and
  client retries; expand/contract migrations so both versions run against one
  schema; rollout undo rehearsed.
